Original bug 19: a co-op creature's auto-target check compares its distance to the other player with the current
auto-target's distance to player 1, and writes the slot before turning off a dead target. The fix, in co-op,
measures both from the finally targeted player, after the redirection. Under both policies, a reevaluation whose
other player is dead compares the targeted player's distance, as Python does, where native reads an uninitialized
stack local.
--- a/decomp/1.9/crimsonland/crimsonland/creature_update_all.cpp
+++ b/decomp/1.9/crimsonland/crimsonland/creature_update_all.cpp
@@ -230,6 +230,10 @@
                                     creatures[creature_index].target_player =
                                         1 - target_player_slot;
                                 }
+                            } else {
+                                // Native compares stack residue here; Python, and so both policies, the
+                                // targeted player's own distance.
+                                alternate_distance = distance;
                             }
                         } else {
                             alternate_distance = vec2_distance(
@@ -240,7 +244,8 @@
                         target_player_slot =
                             creatures[creature_index].target_player;
                         target_player_index = (int)target_player_slot;
-                        if (alternate_distance < vec2_distance(
+                        if ((portable_preserve_bugs || config_player_count != 2)
+                            && alternate_distance < vec2_distance(
                                 &player_state_table[0].position,
                                 &creature_pool[
                                     player_state_table[target_player_index].auto_target
@@ -252,6 +257,17 @@
                     if (player_state_table[target_player_index].health <= 0.0f) {
                         creatures[creature_index].target_player =
                             1 - target_player_slot;
+                    }
+
+                    if (!portable_preserve_bugs && config_player_count == 2
+                        && creature_update_tick % 70 != 0) {
+                        player_state_t *targeted =
